// Enemies, ported from benilla-app's survivors/data.rs. `display` is the CreatureDisplayInfo id
// (the model). `speed` in yards/second, `damage` per swing, `xp` per kill. `radius` is the body size
// before `scale` (default 0.6; 1.3 for the great beasts). Health, damage and experience come from
// each creature's place on its zone's list, read off The Barrens' tuned ladder (data.rs `ladder()`).
// Creatures whose model is missing from the game data are left out.
// `mechanics` are what its elites and bosses do beyond walking up and swinging (Charge, Caster,
// Slam, Leap, Frenzy, Healer, Summoner, and the bosses' Patches and DeathGrip; see
// crates/together-sim/src/mechanics.rs); ordinary enemies never use them. A boss's `hint` is the
// sentence under its bar. A boss's own `hp` is not used: bosses, champions and elites take their
// health from rules.ron (`boss_health`, `champion_health`, `elite_health`).
